Page program memory map
Cells zero to forty seven hold flags and scratch values as follows
zero run flag; one header phase; two header counter; three name active; four first name byte;
five reprocess; six need read; seven alive; eight at sign test; ten component use; eleven layout paused;
thirteen sweep status copy; sixteen duplicate; eighteen status advanced test; nineteen name active copy;
twenty stop accumulator; twenty one not stop; twenty two equality temporary; twenty three paren test;
twenty four not at sign for name; twenty five at sign copy; twenty six literal flag; twenty seven not at sign;
twenty nine component use copy; thirty header use; thirty one single status sum; thirty three skip phase;
thirty four component suffix flag; thirty five emit phase; thirty six argument phase; thirty seven argument output;
thirty eight suffix phase; thirty nine loop flag; forty end of input layout flag; forty one temporary;
forty two paren copy; forty three status zero; forty four status two; forty five to forty seven temporaries and emit loop flag
Cells forty eight to sixty three hold the name register with pad value one
Cell sixty four is the IO cell; cells sixty five to seventy one and seventy three are zero scratch
Cell seventy two is the HOME marker and cell seventy four is the sweep status
Sweeps and the loader are separate modules joined in the order listed by the order file

Page program part 1
Entry pointer on cell zero for part one and on cell sixty four for later parts
Exit pointer on cell sixty four before a sweep and on cell zero after the program
Part boundaries fall exactly where a sweep module is joined in the order file

